{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a prompt box that returns an image."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a TanStack Start app. Then generate an image with OpenRouter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This tutorial is React + Start. For other frameworks, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":". For sizes and other providers, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/image-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can skip the scaffold and paste a key in the sandbox at the end of this page."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-create-a-start-app","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Create a Start app"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npx @tanstack/cli@latest create","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick React. For more options, see "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start getting started"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then install the TanStack AI packages:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-react\",\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get an OpenRouter key from "},{"type":"link","href":"https://openrouter.ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"openrouter.ai"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-and-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client and server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An image generation has two sides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client"}]},{"type":"text","value":" runs in the browser. It holds the key, draws the prompt box, and POSTs to your route."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" route reads that key, calls OpenRouter, and streams the image back."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next steps build the client. Then they add the route."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-set-up-byok-on-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Set up BYOK on the client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/lib/byok.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the key in this tab."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineByok, memoryStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-react/byok'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: memoryStorage(),\n  providers: [openrouterByok],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/components/open-router-key-form.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":". Export "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OpenRouterKeyForm"},{"type":"text","value":" from that file. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.update"},{"type":"text","value":" saves the key. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useByok"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the status."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { useByok } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nexport function OpenRouterKeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n  const [error, setError] = useState('')\n  const status = snapshot.status[openrouterByok.id]\n  const masked = status && 'masked' in status ? status.masked : undefined\n  const missingKey = snapshot.prompt?.reason === 'missing'\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        const next = draft.trim()\n        if (!next) return\n        setError('')\n        void byok\n          .update(openrouterByok.id, next)\n          .then(() => setDraft(''))\n          .catch((caught: unknown) =>\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : 'Could not save key',\n            ),\n          )\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder={masked ? `Saved ${masked}` : 'Paste your OpenRouter key'}\n        value={draft}\n        onChange={(event) => setDraft(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>\n        Save key\n      </button>\n      {missingKey ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key, then generate again.</p>\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want passkeys, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-hook-up-usegenerateimage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Hook up "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/index.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":". Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OpenRouterKeyForm"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@/components/open-router-key-form"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok"},{"type":"text","value":". The hook sends the key in an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" header."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useGenerateImage } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\n// OpenRouter returns a public URL or raw base64. <img src> accepts both.\nfunction imageSrc(image: { url?: string; b64Json?: string }) {\n  if (image.url) return image.url\n  if (image.b64Json) return `data:image/png;base64,${image.b64Json}`\n  return undefined\n}\n\nfunction ImagePage() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  // POST { prompt } to /api/generate/image over SSE.\n  // byok sends the OpenRouter key as x-byok-openrouter.\n  // When the stream ends, result.images holds the picture.\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, stop } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n    byok,\n  })\n\n  const handleGenerate = () => {\n    const next = prompt.trim()\n    if (!next) return\n    void generate({ prompt: next })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {result?.images[0] ? (\n        <img\n          src={imageSrc(result.images[0])}\n          alt={prompt.trim() || 'Generated image'}\n        />\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <textarea\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleGenerate}\n        disabled={!prompt.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: ImagePage,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate({ prompt })"},{"type":"text","value":" starts the run. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.images"},{"type":"text","value":" holds the image when it arrives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A generate with no key does not POST. The form shows \"Paste an OpenRouter key, then generate again.\""}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"bonus-transform-result-with-onresult","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bonus: transform "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":" is the full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerationResult"},{"type":"text","value":". You still pick a URL or base64 for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<img>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"},{"type":"text","value":". Return a src string. The hook then stores that string on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useGenerateImage } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nfunction ImagePage() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  // POST { prompt } to /api/generate/image over SSE.\n  // onResult runs when the image arrives. The return value becomes `result`.\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, stop } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n    byok,\n    onResult: (raw) => {\n      const image = raw.images[0]\n      if (image?.url) return image.url\n      if (image?.b64Json) return `data:image/png;base64,${image.b64Json}`\n      return null\n    },\n  })\n\n  const handleGenerate = () => {\n    const next = prompt.trim()\n    if (!next) return\n    void generate({ prompt: next })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {result ? (\n        <img src={result} alt={prompt.trim() || 'Generated image'} />\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <textarea\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleGenerate}\n        disabled={!prompt.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: ImagePage,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A returned string replaces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":". A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" return keeps the previous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server route does not change."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-add-the-server-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Add the server route"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/api.generate.image.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes"},{"type":"text","value":" folder, next to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":". Start maps that file name to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/api/generate/image"},{"type":"text","value":" path. Do this in two steps."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"read-the-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getByokKey"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-openrouter"},{"type":"text","value":" header, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" in the environment. If both are empty, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokMissing"},{"type":"text","value":" returns HTTP 401."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { generationParamsFromRequest } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  await generationParamsFromRequest('image', request)\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n\n  return new Response('ok')\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/image')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a stub. The next step replaces the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ok"},{"type":"text","value":" body."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openrouterByok"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok"},{"type":"text","value":", not from the adapter main entry."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"call-generateimage-and-return-the-stream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage"},{"type":"text","value":" and return the stream"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ok"},{"type":"text","value":" response. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generationParamsFromRequest"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the prompt from the POST body. Pass the key into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenRouterImage"},{"type":"text","value":". Wrap "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":" so the hook can listen."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  generateImage,\n  generationParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createOpenRouterImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  // Unwrap the prompt the hook POSTed. Then read the OpenRouter key.\n  const { input, threadId, runId } = await generationParamsFromRequest(\n    'image',\n    request,\n  )\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n  if (typeof input.prompt !== 'string') {\n    return new Response('This route accepts a text prompt only.', {\n      status: 400,\n    })\n  }\n\n  // Call OpenRouter. stream: true so the hook can listen on SSE.\n  // The hook stores the finished picture on result.images.\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: createOpenRouterImage('google/gemini-nano-banana-2.1', apiKey),\n    prompt: input.prompt,\n    stream: true,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/image')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This route accepts a text prompt only. OpenRouter returns one image per request."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-try-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Try it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the app. Paste an OpenRouter key. Type a prompt. Click Generate. The image appears."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same app is on the Examples tab at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/ai/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/generate-image"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"client-example","attributes":{"library":"ai","framework":"react","slug":"generate-image"},"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have an image from a prompt. The OpenRouter key never sits in a server env file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full example is on GitHub: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/react/generate-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack/ai "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/react/generate-image"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For sizes, image-to-image, and other providers, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/image-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-create-a-start-app","text":"1. Create a Start app","level":2},{"id":"client-and-server","text":"Client and server","level":2},{"id":"2-set-up-byok-on-the-client","text":"2. Set up BYOK on the client","level":2},{"id":"3-hook-up-usegenerateimage","text":"3. Hook up useGenerateImage","level":2},{"id":"bonus-transform-result-with-onresult","text":"Bonus: transform result with onResult","level":2},{"id":"4-add-the-server-route","text":"4. Add the server route","level":2},{"id":"read-the-key","text":"Read the key","level":3},{"id":"call-generateimage-and-return-the-stream","text":"Call generateImage and return the stream","level":3},{"id":"5-try-it","text":"5. Try it","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want a prompt box that returns an image.\n\nCreate a TanStack Start app. Then generate an image with OpenRouter.\n\nThis tutorial is React + Start. For other frameworks, open [Quick Start](../getting-started/quick-start). For sizes and other providers, open [Image Generation](../media/image-generation).\n\nYou can skip the scaffold and paste a key in the sandbox at the end of this page.\n\n## 1. Create a Start app\n\n```bash\nnpx @tanstack/cli@latest create\n```\n\nPick React. For more options, see [Start getting started](https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/quick-start).\n\nThen install the TanStack AI packages:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openrouter\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nGet an OpenRouter key from [openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai).\n\n## Client and server\n\nAn image generation has two sides.\n\nThe **client** runs in the browser. It holds the key, draws the prompt box, and POSTs to your route.\n\nThe **server** route reads that key, calls OpenRouter, and streams the image back.\n\nThe next steps build the client. Then they add the route.\n\n## 2. Set up BYOK on the client\n\nCreate `src/lib/byok.ts`. `memoryStorage()` keeps the key in this tab.\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineByok, memoryStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-react/byok'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: memoryStorage(),\n  providers: [openrouterByok],\n})\n```\n\nCreate `src/components/open-router-key-form.tsx`. Export `OpenRouterKeyForm` from that file. `byok.update` saves the key. `useByok` reads the status.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { useByok } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nexport function OpenRouterKeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n  const [error, setError] = useState('')\n  const status = snapshot.status[openrouterByok.id]\n  const masked = status && 'masked' in status ? status.masked : undefined\n  const missingKey = snapshot.prompt?.reason === 'missing'\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        const next = draft.trim()\n        if (!next) return\n        setError('')\n        void byok\n          .update(openrouterByok.id, next)\n          .then(() => setDraft(''))\n          .catch((caught: unknown) =>\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : 'Could not save key',\n            ),\n          )\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder={masked ? `Saved ${masked}` : 'Paste your OpenRouter key'}\n        value={draft}\n        onChange={(event) => setDraft(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>\n        Save key\n      </button>\n      {missingKey ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key, then generate again.</p>\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIf you want passkeys, open [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## 3. Hook up `useGenerateImage`\n\nOpen `src/routes/index.tsx`. Import `OpenRouterKeyForm` from `@/components/open-router-key-form`. Pass `byok`. The hook sends the key in an `x-byok-*` header.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useGenerateImage } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\n// OpenRouter returns a public URL or raw base64. <img src> accepts both.\nfunction imageSrc(image: { url?: string; b64Json?: string }) {\n  if (image.url) return image.url\n  if (image.b64Json) return `data:image/png;base64,${image.b64Json}`\n  return undefined\n}\n\nfunction ImagePage() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  // POST { prompt } to /api/generate/image over SSE.\n  // byok sends the OpenRouter key as x-byok-openrouter.\n  // When the stream ends, result.images holds the picture.\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, stop } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n    byok,\n  })\n\n  const handleGenerate = () => {\n    const next = prompt.trim()\n    if (!next) return\n    void generate({ prompt: next })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {result?.images[0] ? (\n        <img\n          src={imageSrc(result.images[0])}\n          alt={prompt.trim() || 'Generated image'}\n        />\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <textarea\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleGenerate}\n        disabled={!prompt.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: ImagePage,\n})\n```\n\n`generate({ prompt })` starts the run. `result.images` holds the image when it arrives.\n\nA generate with no key does not POST. The form shows \"Paste an OpenRouter key, then generate again.\"\n\n## Bonus: transform `result` with `onResult`\n\n`result` is the full `ImageGenerationResult`. You still pick a URL or base64 for `<img>`.\n\nPass `onResult`. Return a src string. The hook then stores that string on `result`.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useGenerateImage } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nfunction ImagePage() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  // POST { prompt } to /api/generate/image over SSE.\n  // onResult runs when the image arrives. The return value becomes `result`.\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, stop } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n    byok,\n    onResult: (raw) => {\n      const image = raw.images[0]\n      if (image?.url) return image.url\n      if (image?.b64Json) return `data:image/png;base64,${image.b64Json}`\n      return null\n    },\n  })\n\n  const handleGenerate = () => {\n    const next = prompt.trim()\n    if (!next) return\n    void generate({ prompt: next })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {result ? (\n        <img src={result} alt={prompt.trim() || 'Generated image'} />\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <textarea\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleGenerate}\n        disabled={!prompt.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: ImagePage,\n})\n```\n\nA returned string replaces `result`. A `null` return keeps the previous `result`.\n\nThe server route does not change.\n\n## 4. Add the server route\n\nCreate `src/routes/api.generate.image.ts` in the `src/routes` folder, next to `index.tsx`. Start maps that file name to the `/api/generate/image` path. Do this in two steps.\n\n### Read the key\n\n`getByokKey` reads the `x-byok-openrouter` header, then `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in the environment. If both are empty, `byokMissing` returns HTTP 401.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { generationParamsFromRequest } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  await generationParamsFromRequest('image', request)\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n\n  return new Response('ok')\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/image')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis is a stub. The next step replaces the `ok` body.\n\nImport `openrouterByok` from `@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok`, not from the adapter main entry.\n\n### Call `generateImage` and return the stream\n\nReplace the `ok` response. `generationParamsFromRequest` reads the prompt from the POST body. Pass the key into `createOpenRouterImage`. Wrap `generateImage()` with `toServerSentEventsResponse`. Pass `stream: true` so the hook can listen.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  generateImage,\n  generationParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createOpenRouterImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  // Unwrap the prompt the hook POSTed. Then read the OpenRouter key.\n  const { input, threadId, runId } = await generationParamsFromRequest(\n    'image',\n    request,\n  )\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n  if (typeof input.prompt !== 'string') {\n    return new Response('This route accepts a text prompt only.', {\n      status: 400,\n    })\n  }\n\n  // Call OpenRouter. stream: true so the hook can listen on SSE.\n  // The hook stores the finished picture on result.images.\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: createOpenRouterImage('google/gemini-nano-banana-2.1', apiKey),\n    prompt: input.prompt,\n    stream: true,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/image')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis route accepts a text prompt only. OpenRouter returns one image per request.\n\n## 5. Try it\n\nRun the app. Paste an OpenRouter key. Type a prompt. Click Generate. The image appears.\n\nThe same app is on the Examples tab at `/ai/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/generate-image`.\n\n<!-- ::client-example library=ai framework=react slug=generate-image -->\n\nYou have an image from a prompt. The OpenRouter key never sits in a server env file.\n\nThe full example is on GitHub: [TanStack/ai `examples/react/generate-image`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/react/generate-image).\n\nFor sizes, image-to-image, and other providers, open [Image Generation](../media/image-generation).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Generate Image\nid: generate-image\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Create a TanStack Start app, then add React image generation. BYOK holds the OpenRouter key in the tab. useGenerateImage talks to a server route that runs generateImage.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - tutorial\n  - generate image\n  - useGenerateImage\n  - generateImage\n  - byok\n  - openrouter\n  - tanstack start\n---\n\nYou want a prompt box that returns an image.\n\nCreate a TanStack Start app. Then generate an image with OpenRouter.\n\nThis tutorial is React + Start. For other frameworks, open [Quick Start](../getting-started/quick-start). For sizes and other providers, open [Image Generation](../media/image-generation).\n\nYou can skip the scaffold and paste a key in the sandbox at the end of this page.\n\n## 1. Create a Start app\n\n```bash\nnpx @tanstack/cli@latest create\n```\n\nPick React. For more options, see [Start getting started](https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/quick-start).\n\nThen install the TanStack AI packages:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openrouter\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nGet an OpenRouter key from [openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai).\n\n## Client and server\n\nAn image generation has two sides.\n\nThe **client** runs in the browser. It holds the key, draws the prompt box, and POSTs to your route.\n\nThe **server** route reads that key, calls OpenRouter, and streams the image back.\n\nThe next steps build the client. Then they add the route.\n\n## 2. Set up BYOK on the client\n\nCreate `src/lib/byok.ts`. `memoryStorage()` keeps the key in this tab.\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineByok, memoryStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-react/byok'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: memoryStorage(),\n  providers: [openrouterByok],\n})\n```\n\nCreate `src/components/open-router-key-form.tsx`. Export `OpenRouterKeyForm` from that file. `byok.update` saves the key. `useByok` reads the status.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { useByok } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nexport function OpenRouterKeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n  const [error, setError] = useState('')\n  const status = snapshot.status[openrouterByok.id]\n  const masked = status && 'masked' in status ? status.masked : undefined\n  const missingKey = snapshot.prompt?.reason === 'missing'\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        const next = draft.trim()\n        if (!next) return\n        setError('')\n        void byok\n          .update(openrouterByok.id, next)\n          .then(() => setDraft(''))\n          .catch((caught: unknown) =>\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : 'Could not save key',\n            ),\n          )\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder={masked ? `Saved ${masked}` : 'Paste your OpenRouter key'}\n        value={draft}\n        onChange={(event) => setDraft(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>\n        Save key\n      </button>\n      {missingKey ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key, then generate again.</p>\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIf you want passkeys, open [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## 3. Hook up `useGenerateImage`\n\nOpen `src/routes/index.tsx`. Import `OpenRouterKeyForm` from `@/components/open-router-key-form`. Pass `byok`. The hook sends the key in an `x-byok-*` header.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useGenerateImage } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\n// OpenRouter returns a public URL or raw base64. <img src> accepts both.\nfunction imageSrc(image: { url?: string; b64Json?: string }) {\n  if (image.url) return image.url\n  if (image.b64Json) return `data:image/png;base64,${image.b64Json}`\n  return undefined\n}\n\nfunction ImagePage() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  // POST { prompt } to /api/generate/image over SSE.\n  // byok sends the OpenRouter key as x-byok-openrouter.\n  // When the stream ends, result.images holds the picture.\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, stop } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n    byok,\n  })\n\n  const handleGenerate = () => {\n    const next = prompt.trim()\n    if (!next) return\n    void generate({ prompt: next })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {result?.images[0] ? (\n        <img\n          src={imageSrc(result.images[0])}\n          alt={prompt.trim() || 'Generated image'}\n        />\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <textarea\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleGenerate}\n        disabled={!prompt.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: ImagePage,\n})\n```\n\n`generate({ prompt })` starts the run. `result.images` holds the image when it arrives.\n\nA generate with no key does not POST. The form shows \"Paste an OpenRouter key, then generate again.\"\n\n## Bonus: transform `result` with `onResult`\n\n`result` is the full `ImageGenerationResult`. You still pick a URL or base64 for `<img>`.\n\nPass `onResult`. Return a src string. The hook then stores that string on `result`.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useGenerateImage } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nfunction ImagePage() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  // POST { prompt } to /api/generate/image over SSE.\n  // onResult runs when the image arrives. The return value becomes `result`.\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, stop } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n    byok,\n    onResult: (raw) => {\n      const image = raw.images[0]\n      if (image?.url) return image.url\n      if (image?.b64Json) return `data:image/png;base64,${image.b64Json}`\n      return null\n    },\n  })\n\n  const handleGenerate = () => {\n    const next = prompt.trim()\n    if (!next) return\n    void generate({ prompt: next })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {result ? (\n        <img src={result} alt={prompt.trim() || 'Generated image'} />\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <textarea\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleGenerate}\n        disabled={!prompt.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: ImagePage,\n})\n```\n\nA returned string replaces `result`. A `null` return keeps the previous `result`.\n\nThe server route does not change.\n\n## 4. Add the server route\n\nCreate `src/routes/api.generate.image.ts` in the `src/routes` folder, next to `index.tsx`. Start maps that file name to the `/api/generate/image` path. Do this in two steps.\n\n### Read the key\n\n`getByokKey` reads the `x-byok-openrouter` header, then `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in the environment. If both are empty, `byokMissing` returns HTTP 401.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { generationParamsFromRequest } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  await generationParamsFromRequest('image', request)\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n\n  return new Response('ok')\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/image')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis is a stub. The next step replaces the `ok` body.\n\nImport `openrouterByok` from `@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok`, not from the adapter main entry.\n\n### Call `generateImage` and return the stream\n\nReplace the `ok` response. `generationParamsFromRequest` reads the prompt from the POST body. Pass the key into `createOpenRouterImage`. Wrap `generateImage()` with `toServerSentEventsResponse`. Pass `stream: true` so the hook can listen.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  generateImage,\n  generationParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createOpenRouterImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  // Unwrap the prompt the hook POSTed. Then read the OpenRouter key.\n  const { input, threadId, runId } = await generationParamsFromRequest(\n    'image',\n    request,\n  )\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n  if (typeof input.prompt !== 'string') {\n    return new Response('This route accepts a text prompt only.', {\n      status: 400,\n    })\n  }\n\n  // Call OpenRouter. stream: true so the hook can listen on SSE.\n  // The hook stores the finished picture on result.images.\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: createOpenRouterImage('google/gemini-nano-banana-2.1', apiKey),\n    prompt: input.prompt,\n    stream: true,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/image')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis route accepts a text prompt only. OpenRouter returns one image per request.\n\n## 5. Try it\n\nRun the app. Paste an OpenRouter key. Type a prompt. Click Generate. The image appears.\n\nThe same app is on the Examples tab at `/ai/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/generate-image`.\n\n<!-- ::client-example library=ai framework=react slug=generate-image -->\n\nYou have an image from a prompt. The OpenRouter key never sits in a server env file.\n\nThe full example is on GitHub: [TanStack/ai `examples/react/generate-image`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/react/generate-image).\n\nFor sizes, image-to-image, and other providers, open [Image Generation](../media/image-generation).\n"}
